Gave the `documentByline` block a stylesheet. It had none anywhere in `src/theme/`, so on a page it started flush against the viewport edge while every other block sat in the centred content column. The three fields are now inline, separated by a dash, at the small type step, with author names comma-separated; the byline also reads author first, then published, then modified, and its rows are paragraphs rather than nested containers. @ericof
